codemap 8
path feature-repin
kind flow
author ai
group features/cli
note repin [rev]: re-pin every stale step by following its text from revision rev, by default the parent revision (@- in jj, HEAD in git). After a rebase, rev is the change's pre-rebase commit. For each stale step the file is read as rev had it, the step's slice is found there by its stored hash, and the slice with a few lines of context is aligned against every symbol of the step's name, in its own file first and in every file when the symbol left it. A step that keeps at least half its lines is pinned to where they went; the rest stay stale with the reason printed, for path-pin by hand. The output is the review: every re-pinned step whose text changed prints its removed and added lines, and its note has to be reread against them, because a re-pin keeps the note whether or not it still describes the code. The map is saved only when at least one step was re-pinned.

